course: dictionary
lesson: 1955
title: Companion
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A companion is a person or animal you spend time with or travel with. Think of it as a friend who keeps you company. «The Mole had spent the day on the river with some companions.» The companions were the friends who were with him on the river.
explain: Context clues help you work out the meaning. «Horses are herd animals: running away together kept wild horses safe, and a horse kept alone gets stressed, so it needs a companion.» The clue is "kept alone gets stressed": a companion is something that stops a horse feeling alone. Companions can be animals, not only people.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If "a friend who keeps you company" still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A companion can be a person, or an animal such as a dog or a horse.
fact: «Companion» means a friend who keeps you company, or someone you travel with.
fact: Some companions are paid to live with and help an older or ill person.
fact: Companion plants grow well together in a garden.
fact: Dolphins seem to remember old companions' whistles for 20 years or more.
exercise: «The Mole had spent the day on the river with some companions.» Who were the Mole's companions? | The boats he sold at the market | The fish that lived in the river | *The friends who were with him on the river | The Rat's enemies
exercise: In a garden, what are companion plants? | Plants that are paid to help the gardener | Plants that must never be watered | *Plants that grow well together | Plants that only grow in the dark
exercise: Why does a horse kept alone need a companion? | *Being alone makes it stressed | It cannot find any grass to eat | It likes to sleep standing up | It is too small to ride
test: What is a companion? | A large boat on a river | A kind of flower that never grows | A winter coat | *A person or animal you spend time with
test: «He had a faithful companion at his side, a dog named Bruno.» What does companion mean here? | A dog that is for sale | A dog that is too old to walk | *A friend who goes everywhere with him | A dog that has run away
exam: Which means a person paid to live with and help an older or ill person? | A visitor who comes once a year | *A live-in companion | A guard at the gate | A tutor who teaches at school
